{"id": "EUVD-2026-89433", "enisaUuid": "db634572-7157-3bdf-b116-b2319050f446", "description": "U-Boot before 2026.10-rc5 contains a buffer overflow in nfs_read_reply() function in net/nfs-common.c that allows attackers to corrupt memory by supplying crafted NFS READ reply lengths. A malicious NFS server can exploit signed integer handling to bypass length validation and write far past the destination buffer, crashing the bootloader or corrupting memory.", "datePublished": "2026-09-29T21:29:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-30T14:04:58", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot/commit/0bbf09859658b8cc9ac13be41af23b516b8ef69a", "https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot/blob/v2026.07/net/nfs-common.c#L695", "https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/u-boot-before-2026.10-rc5-buffer-overflow-via-nfs-read-reply"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74220", "GHSA-63gj-h865-3h3j"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e3798480-d05f-3ad0-80d2-453e92aa3c46", "product": {"name": "U-Boot", "vendor": {"name": "DENX Software Engineering"}}, "product_version": "0 <2026.10-rc5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9c2019f2-7f3a-3536-94c2-bdf097685242", "vendor": {"name": "U-Boot"}}], "isExploited": false}